[B]About[/B]

This is an unofficial CyanogenMod 7 (Android 2.3.7 Gingerbread) build for the [B]LG Optimus Pro C660 / C660h[/B] (muscat, Qualcomm MSM7227T, ARMv6, 240x320). It is built from the CyanogenMod 7 sources with the C660 device tree adjusted to build cleanly today and a rebuilt 2.6.35 kernel.

[COLOR="Red"][B]Beta build, tested on a single unit. Read the status list before flashing. MMS does not work, and the speaker/earpiece were silent on my unit (see below).[/B][/COLOR]

[SIZE="4"][B]Current status — Beta[/B][/SIZE]

Build: [B]cm-7-20261110-UNOFFICIAL-c660.zip[/B]
Kernel: 2.6.35.10-cyanogenmod
Size: 85158211 bytes (81.2 MB)
MD5: [B]8a7c8e4bd10b82a755a98160c6ccf3cc[/B]

[SIZE="4"][B]What's working[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Basics:[/B] boot, reboot, power off, sleep and wake, launcher
[*][B]Display / GPU:[/B] hardware compositing (SurfaceFlinger), 3D gallery
[*][B]Keyboard:[/B] the physical QWERTY keyboard, with the ghost-key filter in the kernel driver
[*][B]Sensors:[/B] accelerometer and compass with real data
[*][B]Wi-Fi:[/B] scan, connect, browse
[*][B]Bluetooth:[/B] works, device discovery is stable
[*][B]Camera:[/B] preview and photos up to 2048x1536 with correct colours, and video recording with correct colours
[*][B]FM radio:[/B] works
[*][B]SIM / mobile network:[/B] with a working SIM (tested with Movistar Peru) Android reads it, registers on HSDPA and mobile data works; outgoing calls connect and SMS can be sent and received
[*][B]Wi-Fi hotspot / tethering:[/B] a second phone connected to the hotspot and browsed over the mobile data
[*][B]Audio:[/B] headphone output (MP3 and FM radio) and voice calls through a wired headset, in both directions
[*][B]Charging with the phone off:[/B] charger animation without flicker
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Partly done / untested[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Network-locked SIMs:[/B] if the SIM is locked to another operator (it was on one of mine), Android reports it as "network locked" and asks for the unlock code instead of showing a silent "no service"
[*][B]Clock:[/B] the modem only returns a wrong date, so the time must be set by hand until a network gives NITZ
[*][B]GPS:[/B] one session, no fix; it probably needs mobile data
[*][B]Loudspeaker and earpiece:[/B] on my unit they were silent even though the audio HAL routes them without errors, so I believe it is that unit's hardware (not tested with the stock ROM). Please report how yours behaves.
[*][B]A2DP and HFP:[/B] not tested
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Known issues[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]The first boot takes around 30 seconds to reach the launcher. That is normal on this phone: the CPU is locked to the performance governor at 800 MHz, and it must stay that way (the charger animation depends on it).
[*]Waking the screen takes about 0.4 s: the Ilitek panel needs its full init on every wake.
[*][B]MMS does not work.[/B] Movistar Peru no longer seems to provide MMS, so I could not test it with a valid APN.
[*]Some extra SMD channels (DATA8/9/12/13/14) fail to open in the radio log. It is modem noise, harmless.
[/LIST]

